WEBVTT

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.200
(GONG CRASHES)

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.000
Guido, look. Ferraris and tires.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.120
-Let's go!
-Ho-ho! Look at this.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.400
OK, now, Mater, remember,
best behavior.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.800
-You got it, buddy. Hey, what's that?
-Mater!

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.240
Hey, McQueen! Over here.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.480
-Lewis!
-Hey, man.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.120
-Jeff!
-Hey, Lightning.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.920
Can you believe this party?

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.320
Hey.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.800
You done good. You got all the leaves.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:49.400
-Check out that tow truck.
-Man, I wonder who that guy's with.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.080
Ah... Will you guys excuse me
just for one little second?

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.160
Ho-ho! Good job!

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.840
Mater!
Listen, this isn't Radiator Springs.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.320
You're just realizing that?

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.720
Oh-ho! That jet lag really done
a number on you.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.400
Mater, things are different over here.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.600
Which means maybe you should,
you know, act a little different, too.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.480
-Different than what?
-Well, just help me out here.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.160
You need help? Shoot!
Why didn't you say so?

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.120
That's what a tow truck does.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.840
-Yeah, I mean...
-Looky there.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.640
It's Mr. San Francisco.
I'll introduce you.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.360
-Mater, no!
-Look at me. I'm helping you already.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.200
Hey, Mr. San Francisco,
I'd like you to meet...

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.360
Ah, Lightning McQueen! Buona sera.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.280
-Nice to meet you, Francesco.
-Nice to meet you, too.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.200
You are very good-looking.
Not as good as I thought, but good.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.200
Excuse me.
Can I get a picture with you?

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.040
Anything for McQueen's friend.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.440
Miss Sally is going to flip
when she sees this.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.560
-(SIGHS)
-She's Lightning McQueen's girlfriend.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.800
-Oooh!
-She's a big fan of yours.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.760
Hey, she has-a good taste.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.200
Mater's prone to exaggeration.
I wouldn't say she's a "big fan".

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.680
You're right. She's a huge fan!

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.600
She goes on and on
about your open wheels.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.960
Mentioning it once doesn't qualify
as going on and on.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.640
Francesco is familiar
with this reaction to Francesco.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.800
Women respect a car
that has-a nothing to hide.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.400
Yeah, er...

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.080
-Let us have a toast.
-Let's.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.120
I dedicate my win tomorrow
to Miss Sally.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.240
Oh. Sorry.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.480
I already dedicated
my win tomorrow to her.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.040
So, if we both do it,
it's really not so special.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.520
-Besides, I don't have a drink.
-I'll go get you one.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.080
Do you mind if I borrow a few bucks
for one of them drinks?

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.560
-They're free.
-Free? Shoot, what am I doing here?

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:35.680
I should probably go keep an eye
on him. See you at the race.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.680
Yes, you will see Francesco,
but not like this.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.440
You will see him like-a this
as he drives away from you.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.040
Ha! That's cute.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.440
You had one of those made up
for all the racers?

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.680
-No.
-(CHUCKLES)

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:50.080
Okay.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.640
-Ciao, McQueen!
-He is so getting beat tomorrow!

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:58.320
PA: Ladies and gentlecars,
Sir Miles Axlerod.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:02.120
It is my absolute honor
to introduce to you

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.360
the competitors in the first ever
World Grand Prix.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.120
From Brazil, Number 8...

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.520
(ELECTRONIC WHIZZING)

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.160
(BLEEPING AND BUZZING)

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.880
-Oh, hello.
-Hello.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.560
A Volkswagen Karmann Ghia
has no radiator.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.360
That's because it's air-cooled.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.160
Great. I'm Agent Shiftwell.
Holley Shiftwell from the Tokyo station.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.320
-I have a message from London.
-Not here.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.320
Try the canapés on the mezzanine.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.000
The lab boys analyzed the photo I sent?
What did they learn about the camera?

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.280
It appears to be
a standard television camera.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:57.520
They said if you could get closer
photos next time that would be great.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.880
This was London's message?

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.160
Oh, no. No, sir.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.960
The oil platforms you were on,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.000
turns out they're sitting on
the biggest oil reserve in the world.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.360
How did we miss that?

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.400
They've scrambled
everyone's satellites.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.720
The Americans discovered it
just before you did.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.720
They placed an agent on that platform
under deep cover.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.000
He was able to get a photo of the car
who's running the entire operation.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.040
Great.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.520
Who is it?
Has anyone seen the photo yet?

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.040
Nope, not yet.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.840
The American is here tonight
to pass it to you.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.440
He'll signal you when he's ready.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.120
Good, good.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.240
Oh, no.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.040
-What is it?
-Change of plan.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.040
-You're meeting the American.
-What? Me?

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.360
Those thugs down there
were on the oil platform.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.480
If they see me,
the mission is compromised.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:46.640
No, I'm technical. I'm in diagnostics.
I'm... I'm not a field agent.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.720
You are now.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.760
(WHISTLING)

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.760
I'll take one of them. Thank you.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:56.400
Never know which one McQueen
will have a hankering for.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.400
Hey. What you got here that's free?
How about that pistachio ice cream?

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:07.080
-No, no, wasabi.
-Same old same old.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.880
What's up with you?
That looks delicious!

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.960
Er...little more, please.
It is free, right?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.160
Keep it coming. A little more.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:20.920
Come on, let's go. It's free.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.840
You're gettin' there. Scoop, scoop.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.560
There ya go!
Now that's a scoop of ice cream!

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.640
(IN JAPANESE)

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.480
My condolences.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.720
And now our last competitor.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.440
Number 95, Lightning McQueen!

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.760
Ka-chow!

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:39.480
Thank you so much for having us,
Sir Axlerod.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:43.080
I really look forward to racing.
This is a great opportunity.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.480
Oh, the pleasure is all ours, Lightning.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.720
You and your team bring
excellence and professionalism

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:49.960
to this competition.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.480
(SCREAMING)

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.120
Somebody get me water! Aah!

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.480
Oh, sweet relief. Sweet relief.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.640
(MUTTERING)

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.880
(CHUCKLING)

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:12.000
Whatever you do,
do not eat the free pistachio ice cream.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:14.480
It has turned.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.800
-(VOICE ECHOES)
-Sir Axlerod, I can explain.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.640
-This is Mater. He's...
-I know him.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.320
This is the bloke that called in
to the television show.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.160
-You're the one I have to thank.
-No, thank you.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.920
This trip's been amazin'.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.360
Ah. He's a little excited, isn't he?

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.840
-Mater!
-But wait, I... Oh, shoot.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:35.160
-Mater.
-Has anyone got a towel?

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.760
Mater, get a hold of yourself.
You're making a scene!

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:42.320
-But I never leak oil. Never.
-Go take care of yourself right now!

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.280
Comin' through! Leakin' oil.
Where's the bathroom? Thank you.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.360
I gotta go. Oh, er...

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.200
Er...

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.280
-(SCREAMING)
-Sorry, ladies.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:01.240
I'm leakin'. I never leak. I never leak.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.040
I never leak, I never leak, I never leak.

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.000
Oh, oh, I never leak. Oooh!

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.120
I never leak, I never leak, never...

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.160
Wow-wee!

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.240
(JAUNTY PIPED MUSIC)

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.880
What in the...?

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.240
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.400
Hey, that tickles!

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.520
(SPEAKS JAPANESE)

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:33.560
(GIGGLES)

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.280
Waaargh!

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:47.720
Okay, McMissile. I'm here.
It's time for the drop.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.280
(BEEPING)

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.840
OK, so, the American has activated
his tracking beacon.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:56.480
Roger that. Move in.

